    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bbpcho/primitive-357-proof-audit/zipball/verified-2026-09-14.1",
    "body": "This release packages the revised manuscript, the dependency-closed proof inputs, the adopted independent checks, and the records of a completed fresh integrated replay. All 65 prior-arithmetic jobs, all 13 sector/interface jobs and all 16 rank/local checks passed in a clean run lasting 50 minutes 47 seconds.\r\n\r\nDownload **PRIMITIVE_357_VERIFIED_RELEASE_2026-09-14_V1.zip** for the complete package. The PDF is also attached separately for reading. GitHub's automatically generated source archives contain only the smaller control repository.\r\n\r\nThe revised paper includes the completed rank argument, the replacement 7-adic kernel witness, the second-dyadic correction, and the obstruction to both true lifts of the residual class at 5. It also corrects the subgroup statement: H0=⟨D2,D3,D4,D5⟩ has odd index, and the enlarged subgroup H1=⟨D2,E,D4,D5⟩ has index coprime to 400, with 5E=D3+D4+3D5. The finite index of H0 remains sufficient for the global logarithmic annihilator.\r\n\r\nThe release replay uses a clean extraction and a new output directory, with access to the old proof directories and the network denied. It requires all 65 prior-arithmetic jobs, the rank/local reconstruction, and 13 sector/interface jobs: the ten original sectors, the V3 integrity/interface check, the independent Hecke input reconstruction and the full Fano resolvent reconstruction. The Fano check reconstructs all 80 CRT primes and checks five additional primes; the degree-42 verifier defaults separately check their saved CRT certificates at three fresh primes each. Every tested input is preserved unchanged when the final verification records are added.\r\n\r\nThe included verifier distinguishes integrity from arithmetic replay:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython3 -B scripts/verify_release.py\r\npython3 -B scripts/verify_release.py --replay \\\r\n  --python /path/to/python-with-sympy-and-flint \\\r\n  --sage-python /path/to/sage-python --gp /path/to/gp \\\r\n  --output-dir /path/to/new-verification-output\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe replay records the specific runtime adaptations for multiprocessing, PARI/GP and Poppler. The PDF compatibility rule accepts one reviewed Poppler 26.04 page-32 extraction hash in addition to the historical hash; the full published PVT PDF hash and all theorem and arithmetic checks remain enforced.\r\n\r\nSee `RUNTIMES.md` and the programs guide in the archive for software requirements and the exact verification scope. The stated published results and identified historical Magma certificates remain premises; this release does not claim a fresh Magma execution or proof-assistant formalization. The manuscript's author field remains to be completed before arXiv submission.\r\n\r\nEarlier sealed archives remain identifiable by their original names and checksums.\r\n\r\nArchive SHA-256: `27e3e6eeb50f83ea484e7cd0c94dbd88de0141ab9f47634ed5181e7db0ecba33` (588,945,520 bytes).\r\n"
